Z||000009||Oreif||04-26-2001||02:32 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BBBAD GT:<BR><B>So do you have to signup in advance or anything, or just show up?  Is it a judging show, or just a basic 'get together'?  Bob's web site doesn't say anything about his show.  Anybody know?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It is just a "get Together". Usually there are many cars there. Free lunch, vendors, (Rodney, and a few others) many parts to buy from Bob. You don't need to sign up just show up. There are usually demonstrations, a Q&A session, Prize raffles, and Archie may be giving rides in a V-8 Fiero since he enjoyed doing it at his shop. There are even a few kit cars and re-bodies to check out.<BR>A good time to be had by all!<P>I think the NIFE raffle car may be down there too. You can purchase tickets from Paul. (See thread about the raffle)<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007047.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007047.html</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 04-26-2001).]||||reg||1
